{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3509","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3509","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3509\",\"parent_revision\":\"fef2ff5a3f5370f365390dae7793ae32477c624f2f4e932b993f796f9e4cbaf5\",\"root_revision\":\"fef2ff5a3f5370f365390dae7793ae32477c624f2f4e932b993f796f9e4cbaf5\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/skills/final-verification/SKILL.md` and the DH stage taxonomy expose only `CERTIFIED` and `NOT_CERTIFIED`. Its tables likewise only allow `YES / NO` and `PASS / FAIL`; the Gaps section conflates an unmet requirement with missing or unsupported evidence. The routing therefore sends both cases directly to corrective task decomposition.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nDefine a third S7 verification outcome, `INCOMPLETE`, for evidence that cannot establish a requested truth (for example, an unavailable or unsupported validation command) without asserting that the requirement is false. Add per-truth and per-quality-gate status values that distinguish `FAIL` from `INCOMPLETE`; preserve the recorded evidence/reason; route `INCOMPLETE` to evidence acquisition, environment remediation, or explicit human decision rather than automatically creating product-change tasks. Keep `CERTIFIED` restricted to fully established evidence and `NOT_CERTIFIED` to demonstrated requirement failure.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. `final-verification/SKILL.md`, the default-flow reference, stage taxonomy, and artifact-conventions reference document `INCOMPLETE` alongside `CERTIFIED` and `NOT_CERTIFIED`.\\n2. A completed S7 artifact can record a goal or quality gate as `INCOMPLETE` with an evidence-gap reason.\\n3. The documented S7 routing for an incomplete result does not create a corrective implementation task until the missing evidence is resolved or a human explicitly decides to treat it as failure.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Source\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nResearch entry: `./research/code-auditing/skylos.md`, \u201cPatterns Worth Adopting\u201d \u2014 preserve an `incomplete` state when requested proof cannot be established rather than treating it as pass.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"8d3642d0baefcebac29a4fdb929f71c2ce7567af3237629dd8a308a9ae7c357e\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABUeT7mA\"}"}